old_concl = r"""In this paper, we localized, mathematically diagnosed, and resolved the post-training quantization collapse of lightweight CNNs in edge-based avian disease diagnosis. We audited public datasets to eliminate optimistic evaluation bias, identifying 617 near-duplicate pairs (156 cross-partition leaks) and establishing an 8,153-image sterile benchmark ($n=1,728$ test samples). Our SQNR formulation proves that cross-channel weight variance ($\Delta_{w,l} \approx 14.8$) in depthwise separable convolutions degrades effective bit-width to $B_{\text{eff}} \le 4.09$ bits and drops depthwise SQNR to 8.4\,dB under per-tensor scaling, inducing complete mode collapse in EfficientNet-B0 (10.42\% accuracy, 97.0\% collapsing into Newcastle Disease). We formulated a static per-channel QDQ calibration protocol that restores diagnostic fidelity across architectures (EfficientNet-B0 to 94.56\%, MobileNetV2 to 97.74\%, and ShuffleNetV2 to 97.57\%). Furthermore, structured channel pruning reveals that structural parameter removal immediately collapses minority sensitivity to 0.0\%, and subsequent unweighted fine-tuning starves the lethal minority class (31.21\% NCD recall at 50\% sparsity); 30-epoch class-weighted loss with FP32 teacher distillation successfully recovers sensitivity to 86.52\% [79.91\%, 91.20\%]. Physical benchmarking on Raspberry Pi 5 under ONNX Runtime 1.29 CPU EP confirmed that static per-channel QDQ fuses into native \texttt{QLinearConv} kernels, unlocking hardware acceleration (7.59\,ms on MobileNetV2, 6.29\,ms on ShuffleNetV2) and dominating the Pareto frontier. Finally, power profiling and boot timing analysis ($t_{\text{boot}} \approx 12.54$\,s) demonstrated that warm-sleep duty cycling sustains over 30 days of autonomous off-grid field surveillance."""

